  "conclusions": [
    "The 21-22/25 MTP5 instability is not explained by corrupted model bytes: fresh direct and ordinary model views passed before every valid run.",
    "TP2 cross-rank oneCCL collectives/allreduce are not necessary for the output instability because a sealed, byte-identical TP1 executable/cache state still produced divergent token arrays. The TP1 process still initialized its world-size-one XCCL backend.",
    "The target-only lane also flipped one long-rollover token, so at least one residual source is not specific to speculative verification.",
    "The 102.13-102.18 tok/s post-recovery arms and the historical 101.170 tok/s anchor remain diagnostic research measurements, not promotable records.",
    "The next correctness step is a bounded same-cache TP1 trace of the structured-extraction divergence, starting at the earliest layer/operator state that can be observed without changing the execution path."
  ]
